cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Murshid, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Murshid: Arabic-first question answering over Saudi government-services FAQs"
abstract: >-
  Retrieval-augmented question answering over a synthetic corpus of Saudi
  government-services FAQs. It answers in the user's register (Modern Standard
  Arabic, Saudi or Gulf dialect, or mixed), quotes its sources verbatim, and
  decides by rules when to answer, answer in part and escalate, refuse, or ask
  for clarification.
authors:
  - given-names: Eslam
    family-names: Hamed
    website: "https://eslamhamed.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Eslam93/Murshid"
url: "https://eslamhamed.com"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
keywords:
  - arabic
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - dialect
  - evaluation
  - saudi
